{"book":65,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"Contend for the Faith","summary":"Jude urges believers to defend the faith against ungodly intruders, recalls examples of God's judgment, and calls the faithful to build themselves up, show mercy, and trust God to keep them.","background":"Jude's examples come from Israel's history (the wilderness, Sodom, Cain, Balaam, Korah) and from Jewish tradition. Verses 14–15 quote 1 Enoch, a Jewish writing not included in the Bible but widely known then. Michael's dispute with the devil over Moses' body (v. 9) is not in the Old Testament and probably comes from another Jewish work.","customs":[{"term":"Feasts of charity","verses":"1:12","note":"Early believers shared 'love feasts', fellowship meals often connected with the Lord's Supper. The intruders were treating them as chances to indulge themselves."},{"term":"Korah's gainsaying","verses":"1:11","note":"'Core' is Korah, who rebelled against Moses and Aaron and was swallowed by the earth (Numbers 16)."}],"watchFor":["Jude loves groups of three: 'mercy… peace… love' (v. 2); Cain, Balaam, Korah (v. 11).","Vivid images from nature: waterless clouds, dead trees, wild waves (vv. 12–13).","One of the Bible's best-loved closing blessings (vv. 24–25)."],"connections":["Numbers 14:29-35","Genesis 19:24","Numbers 16:31-33","Genesis 5:21-24"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Ἰούδας","Ioudas","G2455","N-NSM-P","Jude"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-GSM-P","of Jesus"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","Christ"],["δοῦλος","doulos","G1401","N-NSM","servant"],["ἀδελφὸς","adelphos","G80","N-NSM","brother"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","then"],["Ἰακώβου","Iakōbou","G2385","N-GSM-P","of James"],["τοῖς","tois","G3588","T-DPM","To those"],["ἐν","en","G1722","PREP","in"],["θεῷ","theō","G2316","N-DSM-T","God"],["πατρὶ","patri","G3962","N-DSM-T","[the] Father"],["ἠγαπημένοις","ēgapēmenois","G25","V-RPP-DPM","loved"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-DSM-P","in Jesus"],["Χρι